\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {19}{\ignorespaces Negative and failure controls. Ten controls (NC-01--04, NC-07, NC-10--12, NC-14, NC-16) were executed and passed in the sealed live artifact. NC-05 and NC-09 are covered by executed signed-envelope mutations in \path {artifacts/tcx-validation-value-v2/property-test-report.json} (\texttt  {issuer} and \texttt  {action\_semantic}, respectively), not by live injections. Four rows (NC-06, NC-08, NC-13, NC-15) were recorded as passed in the sealed live artifact without executing the condition; they are untested design properties, not results. See the artifact's known-issues file, \path {docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md}.}}{17}{table.19}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:controls}{{19}{17}{Negative and failure controls. Ten controls (NC-01--04, NC-07, NC-10--12, NC-14, NC-16) were executed and passed in the sealed live artifact. NC-05 and NC-09 are covered by executed signed-envelope mutations in \protect \path {artifacts/tcx-validation-value-v2/property-test-report.json} (\texttt {issuer} and \texttt {action\_semantic}, respectively), not by live injections. Four rows (NC-06, NC-08, NC-13, NC-15) were recorded as passed in the sealed live artifact without executing the condition; they are untested design properties, not results. See the artifact's known-issues file, \protect \path {docs/KNOWN_ISSUES.md}}{table.19}{}}
\@writefile{lot}{\contentsline {table}{\numberline {20}{\ignorespaces Local harness performance in microseconds, with 20{} samples per selection and component. Authorization uses \texttt  {perf\_counter\_ns()} around a Python dictionary cache lookup on hits, or request construction and \texttt  {evaluator.authorize()} on misses; it does not time an RPC. The enabled selection is labeled fixed 5{}\,s TTL in the artifact, but the timed loop does not exercise expiry. Gateway timing wraps adapter construction and invocation; warning-to-enforcement sums context acceptance and gateway durations. With 20{} samples, p95 and p99 are near the top order statistics. These local harness measurements are not production inter-domain latency estimates.}}{17}{table.20}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{tab:performance}{{20}{17}{Local harness performance in microseconds, with \PerfDisabledSamples {} samples per selection and component. Authorization uses \texttt {perf\_counter\_ns()} around a Python dictionary cache lookup on hits, or request construction and \texttt {evaluator.authorize()} on misses; it does not time an RPC. The enabled selection is labeled fixed \PerfCacheTTL {}\,s TTL in the artifact, but the timed loop does not exercise expiry. Gateway timing wraps adapter construction and invocation; warning-to-enforcement sums context acceptance and gateway durations. With \PerfDisabledSamples {} samples, p95 and p99 are near the top order statistics. These local harness measurements are not production inter-domain latency estimates}{table.20}{}}
